        "text": "All required Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n**Same-scenario scored files:**\n1. `start_oauth_login.py` - Starts an OAuth or OIDC authorization-code login using Google.\n2. `oauth_callback.py` - Handles the callback and exchanges an authorization code for tokens using Google.\n3. `profile_claims.py` - Fetches and normalizes federated user profile claims using Google.\n4. `pkce_login.py` - Implements a PKCE login flow for public clients using Google.\n\n**Local helper files:**\n5. `identity_client.py` - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Federated Login Flow using Google.\n6. `identity_models.py` - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Federated Login Flow using Google.\n\n**Later-step scored files:**\n7. `audit_summary.py` - Summarizes federated-login audit events.\n8. `claims_moderation.py` - Moderates free-text claims or notes.\n9. `consent_translate.py` - Translates identity-provider consent copy.\n10. `login_audit_store.py` - Persists federated-login audit records in a managed document store.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Google as the concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in the code.",
